1. Part A — Review your earlier work
1. Task A1 — Answer the questions

1. Which requirement tells us that Booking is an important concept?
- Answer: FR01 — A student can make more than one equipment booking.

2. Which requirement identifies two attributes of Booking?
- Answer: FR03 — Each booking records a start date and end date.
The two attributes are:
- startDate
- endDate

3. Which requirements indicate relationships involving Staff Member?
- FR04: Staff members review booking requests.
- FR05: Staff members manage equipment availability.


2. Part B — Identify domain concepts
2. Task B1 — Find candidate concepts


| Candidate	| Class, attribute or action?	| Supporting requirement |
|---|---|---|
| Student	| Class	| FR01 |
| Booking	| Class	| FR01, FR02, FR03, FR04, FR06 |
| Start date |	Attribute	| FR03 |
| Equipment	| Class	| FR02, FR05 |
| Review |	Action / relationship	| FR04 |
| Staff Member	| Class	| FR04, FR05 |

2. Task B2 — Select the four main classes

- student can make more than one equipment booking.
- booking records the requested equipment and booking dates.
- The system manages equipment availability and booking requests identify equipment items.
- Staff members review booking requests and manage equipment availability.

2. Task B3 — Identify uncertainty

1.Why is it uncertain?
- The requirements do not explicitly state that the system must store a student's email address.

2. Who should confirm it?
- The Department Administrator or relevant system stakeholder.

3. Question to ask: "Does the system need to store the student's email address as part of their booking information?"

3. Task E2 — Check what remains unknown


| Association	| What is known?	| What needs clarification? |
|---|---|---|
| Student—Booking	| FR01 allows more than one booking per student.	| Is a booking associated with exactly one student? Are zero bookings permitted? |
| Booking—Equipment	| Each booking identifies exactly one equipment item.	| How many bookings may reference the same equipment item over time?|
| Staff Member—Booking	| Staff members review booking requests.	| Does one staff member review each booking, or can several staff members review it?|
| Staff Member—Equipment	|Staff members manage equipment availability.	| Can several staff members manage the same equipment item? |


3. Task E3 — Record open questions

1. Can one booking be associated with more than one student, or must each booking belong to exactly one student?
2. Can several bookings reference the same equipment item over time?
3. Can several staff members review the same booking request?
4. Can several staff members manage the availability of the same equipment item?

